  "notes": "Cove kost lobby (preview). Street enter lands here first (njh_door_kos_cove_lobby). Five orange lobby doors along the back wall, matching old VO Cove: rooms 1–3 locked, room 4 Ichsan (njh_door_home_ichsan → njh_kos_ichsan), room 5 Noor (njh_door_home_noor → njh_kos_noor). virtual-life-interior-v1 has no nested-door furniture TYPE, so room and street exits are listed in doors[] (exits[] is the role=exit subset). Sprites are Ellen's pintu_lobi_* from kamar_cove_kosong, copied to interiors/lobby-doors/; they are not catalog TYPEs — Baymax should draw doors[].sprite / doors[].sprites by viewer state (milik / milik_orang_lain / terkunci / tersedia). Preview only.",
  "adaptedFrom": "Ellen kamar_cove_kosong lobby door sprites + Cove lobby geometry in vo-mp/ind/p_cove.py and virtual-office/index.html (r0=24.6, five doors at c -20.5/-18.85/-17.2/-15.55/-13.9, owners index 3 Ichsan / 4 Noor).",
  "schemaNoteForBaymax": "New field: doors[] on an interior scene. Each entry has id, role (room|exit), label, c, r, useTile, usePoint, and for room doors: state, interiorTemplate, ownerId/owner/partnerOwner, access, sprite/sprites. exits[] is the subset with role=exit (street or parent interior). Open room interiors by door id or interiorTemplate; do not open a bedroom from the street door. Street door id is njh_door_kos_cove_lobby."
